  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nUpper trough that has helped bring need rain and thundershowers \nto the Silver State is on its way east toward the central plains. \nUpper level ridge will shift back west and south through the end \nof the week, cutting of the monsoon moisture feed allowing for \nstorm chances to wind down through the weekend. Thursday the ridge\nwill build west, as it re-establishes over the SW US the southern\nflow will shift to Southwesterly flow cutting of our monsoon \nmoisture supply. For Thursday, Friday, and into the weekend see \nshower and storm chances drop each day, as well as coverage \nbecoming more isolated and sparse as dry air shifts west to east, \nculminating with Sunday afternoon being the last chance for storms\nuntil the end of the month. With the drying trend, temperatures \nare set to gradually warm through the weekend with high pressure \nin control. There is one caveat with this scenario, and that is \nexact ridge location, current model shows the ridge keeping the \nmonsoonal flow to our east through next Thursday, but if the ridge\nshifts slightly east storm chances may return to far eastern NV \nas early as Next Tuesday, however confidence is low for this \npossibility.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for decreasing thunderstorm chances each\nafternoon, eventually ending by Sunday afternoon.\n\nThere moderate confidence in the potential for warming \ntemperatures through the weekend as high pressure shifts SW from \nthe southern plains.\n\nThere is low confidence in the return of monsoonal showers as \nearly as Next Tuesday for far eastern NV.",
